message: "If you use Vispectra in academic work, please cite it. This file describes v0.1.1-alpha; the conceptual DOI listed under identifiers always points to the latest archived version."
title: "Vispectra: A compiler for spectroscopic file formats"
abstract: "Vispectra is a cross-platform, browser-based compiler and visualizer for spectroscopic file formats (UV-Vis, XRD, XPS, Raman, IR). It infers the grammatical structure of heterogeneous instrument outputs from a statistical sample of their data, builds a structural contract (the canon), and applies it to the rest. All processing is client-side: zero telemetry, no backend dependencies."
